"https://www.linkedin.com/sales/lead/ACwAAFAqO6cB7WjWwf0mQ8lRwpdBxQkDL0ZnaG0,NAME_SEARCH,MWxF",Wu Haiming,Wu,Haiming,OCBC,Data Engineer,165277,https://www.linkedin.com/sales/company/165277,https://www.linkedin.com/company/165277,"Hi, I’m Wu Haiming - an aspiring software engineer and recent graduate from Singapore Polytechnic with a Diploma in Applied AI and Analytics. My journey into technology began in secondary school, where my curiosity for how systems work evolved into a deep passion for using AI and software to solve real-world problems.

Throughout my academic career, I’ve worked on a wide range of projects-both individually and in teams-covering software development, data analysis, and machine learning. These hands-on experiences have equipped me with a strong foundation in programming, algorithms, and AI concepts. I’m proficient in Python, JavaScript, C++, and SQL, and have built projects using frameworks like TensorFlow, Scikit-learn, and Keras. My experience also includes using tools such as Git, Jupyter Notebooks, and Tableau for visualization and version control.

One of the most formative parts of my learning involved hackathons and group projects, which challenged me to build solutions under pressure and collaborate effectively with teammates. These moments taught me how to communicate ideas clearly, manage time, and remain adaptable-skills that are just as important as writing clean, efficient code.

Before stepping into tech, I worked in retail management at Takashimaya. Managing store operations and customer service helped me develop strong interpersonal skills, problem-solving abilities, and a customer-first mindset. I saw firsthand how technology could streamline operations and enhance customer experience-an insight that continues to shape how I think about building impactful software.

I’m especially interested in how AI can improve systems and decision-making. Whether it's through smarter analytics or better user experiences, I want to be part of teams that create scalable, meaningful solutions.

