"https://www.linkedin.com/sales/lead/ACwAAA96LOoBXWE8Y_vGZluwxzoXvRec9ObNSzw,NAME_SEARCH,piM9",Anbumalar James,Anbumalar,James,Prudential Assurance Company Singapore,Senior Business System Analyst,2140469,https://www.linkedin.com/sales/company/2140469,https://www.linkedin.com/company/2140469,"	18 years of experience in IT as a Techno Business /Data analyst/Product Owner in Banking &amp; Finance, Insurance and Health care domains in software industry with Analysis, Design, Development and Testing experience with Waterfall and Agile (Scrum) methodologies.	Have got strong expertise in requirement gathering and prioritization, business analysis, stake holder management, data mining, data profiling, data gap analysis, impact analysis, Meta data preparation, data mapping, functional specification preparation, data governance, data modelling, maintaining data quality, test management, dashboard and report design. Have got experience with developed use cases &amp; specifications, mapped processes &amp; requirements.Experience in Agile (Scrum) methodology.Certified Scrum Product Owner® (CSPO®). Excellent verbal and written communication skills  Demonstrated experience engaging and influencing senior leaders .Strong experience in Digital Product management .Strong analytical and quantitative skills with the ability to use data and metrics to backup assumptions and Proactively identify and resolve any strategic issues that may impact the team’s ability to meet strategic, financial, and technical goals .Develop and leverage in-depth understanding of business, user, market &amp; competition insights .Leverage insights gathered from data &amp; market to help drive roadmap planning and quarterly goal setting. Proactively present progress against those goals (e.g. dashboard building) to business &amp; platform stakeholders . Define Responsibilities for Production Support and Triage teams within Platform team to manage and resolve incidents/ production defects timely. Ensure that incident reports are filed timely. Ensure that learnings from incidents are baked into preventive steps and proactive monitoring to minimize future disruptions.Ensure adherence to regulatory &amp; compliance requirements .To ensure in-depth understanding of business processes and articulation of use-cases / user-stories for identified features/ capabilities applicable platforms and key transformation for DBS BANCA projects in DBS Singapore.  Guide the teams to Solicit, validate and document business requirements through clear understanding of as-is vs. tobe process, document into user stories with clear acceptance criteria","Prudential’s Future Finance Program (FFP) is a multi-year initiative to modernize its finance function by migrating from SunGL to Oracle ERP for accounting and reporting. The program streamlines bank payments, reconciliation, supplier invoices, and expense processing, while integrating with Standard Chartered Bank (SCB) using Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC), ISO20022, SFTP, and MOVEit. The initiative delivers end-to-end automation, secure financial data exchange, and regulatory compliance across multiple applications.

Key Contributions:

